[Music]  my name is Antony Vitolo I'm the  executive chef at Emilio's bolado on 55  East Houston the veal parmesan that I  make is a staple dish in New York in  Italy it's not really a staple dish it's  more of an American Italian dish you  don't really go to an Italian restaurant  and order veal parmesan but people in  America in New York they like you know  cheese and they love sauce so you know  you have to give the people what they  want  so you have to have veal parmigiana and  chicken parmigiana and an Italian  establishment in New York City it's a  must  veal parm is so special because it's a  different cut of meat it's more tender  and it's more of a gamy flavor it's kind  of like a red and white meat it's like  right in the middle so Bao's my go-to  [Music]  make a veal parmesan you need basically  the right amount of meat of a veal chop  you know the perfect cut of your child  is crazy big or is it 16 ounces so we  pound it out nice and thin nice and flat  so it's the size of the plate then after  you do that you salt and pepper the veal  you know you need to season it and then  you egg wash it I use you know eggs  flour and a little bit of cream it  thickens the batter up it gives like  another inch and then my special panko  bread crumbs I seize them with all  different types of seasoning you know  parsley garlic powder onion powder salt  pepper and the key is pecorino romano  cheese after you bread it I've tried  different ways of making the veal  parmigiana  I've tried deep-frying it but it comes  to crispy the pan fry with the butter  and the extra virgin olive oil gives it  the right amount of crisp that it's not  dry so after you pan fry it you hit it  with tomato sauce while the pan still  hot the red sauce we make it's been  passed down from my father to me  the sauce is special because of the  tomatoes we use our tomatoes we get  imported from Italy then you hit it with  white wine to tenderize the meat a  little bit more the alcohol breaks down  the meat a little bit and then you put  more sauce on top  in my opinion buffalo mozzarella is the  best type of cheese to use when you're  making a parmesan it just melts the best  it's nice and you know moist and it's  just a beautiful cheese and then  obviously you use Parmesan cheese to top  it off on top put it on top of the  salamander and you crisp the edges so  the edges are nice and brown and almost  a black color on around the edges and  the cheese is nice and melted and then  you got that sauce underneath and you  cut through it cuts like butter  we're known for old-school Italian  cuisine and in New York bolaños is the  bread source joint it's not offensive to  me but it's kind of like cheapening like  red sauce joint it's like we make a good  red sauce you know but we want to make  other good things and I learned you know  at a young age for my father that the  freshest ingredients bring out the best  product so no taking shortcuts  everything's fresh our pastas fresh our  meatballs are from scratch our bowling  years is from scratch and that's what  separates us from all the other  restaurants it's all about love and it's  about the passion of the food and I have  the passion and my father has a passion  and with us as a team it's very hard to  compete with the blood family  [Music]

